\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 EXT. SPACE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 An endless field of stars.\
The spiral arms of the Milky Way drift slowly across the screen.\
A tiny vessel emerges from darkness.\
Elegant but practical. Built for exploration rather than combat.\
Hull markings reveal its name:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 USS REPOSITORY
\f1\b0 \
The ship glides silently past the camera.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Captain's Log. Stardate 47.047.\
To explore strange new workflows.\
To seek out new knowledge.\
To boldly document what no one has documented before.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 MUSIC SWELLS.
\f1\b0 \
The USS Repository passes a nebula glowing with the pale blue light of archived data.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Most people think documentation is produced after understanding exists.\
Requirements are gathered.\
Architecture is designed.\
Decisions are made.\
Then someone writes everything down.\
It's a comforting theory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 SOUND:
\f1\b0  A distant computer chirp echoes through space.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 It is also completely wrong.\
The ship passes a derelict communications buoy.\
A faded holographic label blinks:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 FINAL_ARCHITECTURE_v7_APPROVED_FINAL_REALLY_FINAL
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 The longer I captain this ship, the more convinced I become that documentation is often the first signal that nobody understands the system.\
Not the last step.\
The first clue.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 INT. BRIDGE - USS REPOSITORY\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Officers work at stations displaying flowing streams of metadata.\
Lieutenant Commander Yun reviews a wall-sized repository map.\
Every few seconds another branch appears.\
And another.\
And another.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 YUN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 (suspicious)\
Who documented this?\
Nobody answers.\
Yun narrows her eyes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Every mission begins the same way.\
A request appears.\
Update a document.\
Explain a feature.\
Record a decision.\
Review a migration plan.\
The task sounds simple.\
A junior ensign presses a button.\
A dozen contradictory process diagrams appear.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 ENSIGN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Sir... they all claim to be the source of truth.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Of course they do.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Follow the request long enough and you discover something larger.\
A missing owner.\
A forgotten decision.\
A requirement everyone remembers differently.\
A system nobody understands but everyone depends on.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 ALERT CHIME\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 SOUND:
\f1\b0  BOOP-BOOP. BOOP-BOOP.\
The bridge lighting shifts to amber.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 OPERATIONS OFFICER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Captain, we're receiving a distress beacon.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Source?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 OPERATIONS OFFICER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 An archive station.\
Designation: Repository Station 47.\
The bridge falls silent.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 YUN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 That's impossible.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 DAXARA\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Not impossible.\
Merely... poorly documented.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 That station was declared destroyed two centuries ago.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 OPERATIONS OFFICER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Apparently nobody informed the station.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 VIEWSCREEN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 A massive structure slowly rotates into view.\
Ancient.\
Weathered.\
Covered in communications arrays and archive spires.\
Lights still glow behind dormant windows.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Repository Station 47.\
Lost for two hundred years.\
Presumed destroyed.\
Yet somehow still operational.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 SCIENCE OFFICER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Long-range scans indicate active indexing processes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 YUN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Two centuries of continuous maintenance?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 DAXARA\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Interesting.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 SCIENCE OFFICER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 That's not the strange part.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 There's a stranger part?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 SCIENCE OFFICER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Yes, sir.\
The station appears to have gained storage capacity despite receiving no upgrades.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 ...I don't like that.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 VIEWSCREEN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 An incoming transmission appears.\
Origin: UNKNOWN\
Priority: CRITICAL\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 COMPUTER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Incoming message.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 On screen.\
The display flickers.\
Static fills the bridge.\
Then enormous text appears.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 WHO AUTHORIZED DATA DELETION?
\f1\b0 \
The crew exchange uneasy glances.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 DAXARA\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Oh.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 YUN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 That's not a good sign.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 No.\
No, it really isn't.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 COMPUTER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Additional message received.\
The text changes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 WHERE IS THE MISSING LOG?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 MUSIC STINGER\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 A deep orchestral chord.\
The station looms in the viewscreen.\
Silent.\
Waiting.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 CAPTAIN BOB (V.O.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 Officially, our mission is documentation.\
Unofficially, our mission is solving mysteries.\
Something on Repository Station 47 has spent two centuries looking for answers.\
And I have a feeling it's about to start asking questions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

